  # Final review F4 (2026-09-16): a user-defined function named "___" called
  # from a non-variadic function keeps its ordinary meaning (final review
  # probe p1; the existing compat test covers only a local variable). Both
  # placements are pinned: a statement-level call, and a call nested inside
  # another call's argument list -- the latter is where the forwarding token
  # would otherwise hijack the symbol, were it not for the compat gate
  # (findconst/findloc/findglb) in a function without a variable argument
  # list. Inside a variadic function the token wins instead; that consequence
  # is documented in the spec amendment (accepted, F3 in the final review).
